  "structural_conclusion": "The rewind loop is inherently sequential: circuit t+1 depends on result t, so a k-step forecast is k QPU round trips, each dominated by the queue assumption. On the accuracy-vs-latency plane the local simulator (D) and classical surrogate (F) dominate every remote-QPU strategy at this problem size. For a MONTHLY index the horizon latency (minutes) is far inside the decision deadline, so the binding constraint is QPU access/cost, not per-forecast latency.",
